## Provider abstraction

**Go package:** `idp`  
**Import path:** `github.com/usememos/memos/internal/idp`

This package holds the shared cross-protocol user-info type used by all IdP implementations. It does **not** define a Go `interface` for providers; the repo uses a type enum plus protocol-specific packages instead.

```1:8:/bench/repo/internal/idp/idp.go
package idp

type IdentityProviderUserInfo struct {
	Identifier  string
	DisplayName string
	Email       string
	AvatarURL   string
}
```

The schema-level abstraction (provider type + config variant) lives in protobuf:

- **File:** `/bench/repo/proto/store/idp.proto` (lines 7–42)
- **Generated Go package:** `store` at `github.com/usememos/memos/proto/gen/store`

```7:25:/bench/repo/proto/store/idp.proto
message IdentityProvider {
  int32 id = 1;
  string name = 2;

  enum Type {
    TYPE_UNSPECIFIED = 0;
    OAUTH2 = 1;
